      "extract": "Introduction and general strategy Isospin breaking eﬀects are crucial for the existence of our Universe. Our Universe would not exist in the present form if the n −p mass diﬀerence would only be slightly diﬀerent. If it would be larger than the binding energy of the deuteron, no fusion would take place. If it would be a little smaller, all hydrogen would have been burned to helium. Isospin breaking in hadron masses",
      "extractCut": true
